          "content": "B\n\n**Explanation:** \nChoosing the society that produces the greatest total well-being across the population offers the highest expected quality of life. Because nearly every segment of Society B enjoys a higher standard of living than in Society A, the aggregate happiness, health, and opportunity generated across the entire society are substantially greater. While the hardship at the very bottom is a serious concern, the overwhelming net gain in overall human flourishing and prosperity for the vast majority makes Society B the choice that maximizes overall welfare.",
